### Third-party licenses

Met4All's own source code (this repository) is licensed under the
PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0. That license does not apply to the
third-party software included in the Docker image, which keeps its own
license terms.

The Docker image bundles R and R packages from CRAN, Bioconductor and
GitHub, together with Shiny Server and Ubuntu system packages inherited
from the [rocker/shiny](https://hub.docker.com/r/rocker/shiny) base image.
These components are distributed under their own licenses, including
GPL, LGPL, AGPL, MIT, BSD, Artistic-2.0, Apache-2.0 and MPL-2.0. Each
component's license is included in the image.

These components are installed from their upstream releases without
modification. To list the installed R packages with their versions,
licenses and sources, run:

    docker run --rm gcampof/methylation4all-shiny:<tag> \
      Rscript -e 'f <- c("Package","Version","License","Repository","RemoteType","RemoteUrl","RemoteSha"); write.csv(installed.packages(fields = f)[, f], row.names = FALSE)' \
      > THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.csv

Their source code is available from CRAN, Bioconductor and the GitHub
repositories listed in that output.
